:: WalkHomeTogether [nobr] {"position":"2450,3550","size":"100,100"}
/* Generic walk-home dispatcher. Three exit paths:
   1. The active GHOST has a walkHomePassage (haunted-house "something is
      following us" path) -- route there, with a follow-up link.
   2. The active COMPANION is lust>=50: include the catalogue's
      walkHomePassage (eg. BrookWalkHome / AliceWalkHome / BlakeWalkHome).
      That passage owns the lust>=50 sex scene + handoff to whatever
      homeContinuePassage / Sleep target it wants.
   3. Otherwise: shared low-lust "thanks for walking me back" block.
   No companion or ghost name is mentioned anywhere -- per-character copy
   lives in the per-character passages, dispatched via the catalogue. */
<<set _walkHomePassage to setup.ActiveGhost.walkHomePassage()>>
<<set _ac to setup.Companion.active()>>
<<if _walkHomePassage>>
	<<image "ui/img/mchouse.jpg" { width: "100%" }>>
	@@.notmc-speech; I have a strange feeling. Like something is following us...@@<br>
	@@.mc-speech;I didn't see anyone. Maybe you should stay at my place then?@@<br>
	@@.notmc-speech; Yes, if you don't mind.@@<br><br>
	@@.backbtn; <<link "Sleep together" `_walkHomePassage`>>
	<</link>>@@
<<elseif _ac and setup.Companion.lust() gte 50 and _ac.walkHomePassage>>
	<<include _ac.walkHomePassage>>
<<else>>
	<<image "ui/img/mchouse.jpg" { width: "100%" }>>
	@@.mc-speech; We made it to my place. Thanks for walking me back@@<br>
	@@.notmc-speech; No problem, hope we meet again. Bye.@@<br>
	@@.warningtext; (Req. <<= setup.Companion.name()>>'s <<statIcon setup.StatIcon.HEALTH>> ≥ 50)@@
	<br><br>
	@@.backbtn; [[Sleep]]@@<br>
<</if>>

<<run setup.HuntController.markHuntOver()>>
